course: dictionary
lesson: 12758
title: Dwarfism: a word about the body
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Dwarfism is a noun. It names a condition where a person or animal grows much shorter than usual, often because of their genes. Genes are the instructions in our bodies that help decide how we grow. «Her doctor explained that dwarfism can run in some families.» The clues are «doctor» and «genes», so this is a medical matter.
explain: Dwarfism is not a joke. «Mia wrote a school report about dwarfism and asked the class to be kind.» Health lessons use the word to talk about real people with real bodies. Many people with dwarfism prefer words such as «people of short stature» or «a person with dwarfism», so it is polite to listen to what they ask for.
explain: Scientists use the word too, for animals. «On a small island, the deer became much smaller over many generations.» This is island dwarfism: animals on islands become small over many generations. Over time, island dwarfism produced tiny elephants and hippos.
fact: Dwarfism means growing much shorter than usual, often because of genes.
fact: Dwarfism has no plural, so we never say «dwarfisms», and we do not say «a dwarfism».
fact: «Island dwarfism» is when animals on islands become small over many generations.
fact: Island dwarfism produced tiny elephants and hippos in science lessons.
fact: Many people with dwarfism prefer the words «people of short stature» or «a person with dwarfism».
exercise: «Her doctor explained that dwarfism can run in some families.» What does dwarfism mean here? | A fast way of growing tall | A special hospital room | *A condition where a person grows much shorter than usual | A kind of sport played on islands
exercise: «On the island, the deer became much smaller over many generations.» What is this called in science? | *Island dwarfism | Mountain climbing | Island sunshine | Genes
exercise: Ellie laughs at dwarfism in class. What does the lesson tell us about this? | *Dwarfism is a medical condition, not something to laugh at | It shows she is very clever | It is fine, because it is only a word | It means the same as a joke
test: Many people with dwarfism prefer to be described in a certain way. Which phrase do they often prefer? | Tall people | Small kids | *People of short stature | Giants
test: Which sentence uses dwarfism correctly? | A dwarfism is a funny thing. | She has a dwarfism all day. | Dwarfisms are at the zoo. | *Dwarfism can run in some families.
exam: «Her cousin has dwarfism, so the class must be kind about it.» Why is this the right way to think? | *It is a medical condition, so we should laugh at it | It is a medical condition, so we should treat people with respect | It means the cousin lives on an island | It means the cousin is funny
